 Mobile Charities & Nonprofits Help News Tax Pros Search Include Historical Content - Any - No Include Historical Content - Any - No Search Home Instructions 2025 Instructions for Schedule E (Form 1040) (2025)   2025 Instructions for Schedule E (Form 1040) - Introductory Material Future Developments What’s New Standard mileage rate. Bonus depreciation. Increased section 179 deduction dollar limits. Business interest expense limitation. No tax on car loan interest. Reminders Form 7205, Energy Efficient Commercial Buildings Deduction. Excess business loss limitation. Figuring a shareholder’s stock and debt basis. General Instructions Other Schedules and Forms You May Have To File Single-member limited liability company (LLC). Information returns. Qualified Joint Venture (QJV) Making the election. Reportable Transaction Disclosure Statement Limitation on Losses At-Risk Rules Qualified nonrecourse financing. Qualified person. More information. Passive Activity Loss Rules Passive Activity Activities That Are Not Passive Activities Activities of real estate professionals. Other activities. Exception for Certain Rental Real Estate Activities Active participation. Recordkeeping Specific Instructions Filers of Form 1041. Part I Line A Income or Loss From Rental Real Estate and Royalties Personal property. Extraterritorial income exclusion. Chapter 11 bankruptcy cases. Line 1a Line 1b Land rental. Self-rental. Other. Line 2 QJV. Line 3 Rental income from farm production or crop shares. Line 4 General Instructions for Lines 5 Through 21 Renting out part of your home. Credit or deduction for access expenditures. Line 6 Line 10 Lines 12 and 13 Limitation on business interest. How to report. Line 14 Line 17 Line 18 Separating cost of land and buildings. Line 19 Line 21 Line 22 Parts II and III Tax preference items. Part II Income or Loss From Partnerships and S Corporations Special Rules That Limit Losses Basis rules for partnerships. Basis rules for S corporations. At-risk rules